# Expectation record for 06_control_flow/004_switch_edge_cases.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 004_switch_edge_cases
area               = 06_control_flow
description        = Switch edge cases: empty body, default first, default absent, single label, unordered labels, and the dense, offset-dense and sparse label sets that put every dispatch density in front of the backend without requiring any particular lowering -- every label of all three density-sensitive sets printed on its own line under a key naming the input that produced it, in both the constant and the volatile-runtime path, with the two sweep totals kept only as redundant confirmation
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Every controlling value is an integer literal, staged through the volatile int
vin in the runtime variant, and every case label is a distinct integer constant
expression. The widest label magnitude is 1000000 and the widest input magnitude
is 1000000, both far inside the range of a 32-bit int on all four targets, so no
signed overflow is possible. The largest accumulated value is 1720, the sum of
the sixteen dense results, which is likewise far inside range. There is no
shift, no division, no remainder and no pointer arithmetic. Every object is
written before it is read: r is assigned on every reachable path in each helper,
and is pre-initialised in empty_body, default_absent and single_label where a
non-matching value runs no arm at all; the static const input tables have
initialisers; vin is assigned before each read; and every out[] element is
written before it is printed, including the two accumulators which are set to
zero before their sweep loops. No object is modified twice between sequence
points; each volatile write and each volatile read stands in its own statement or
its own controlling expression. There is no aliasing, no address is taken, no
uninitialised storage is read, and nothing depends on padding bytes or on the
relative addresses of unrelated objects. No evaluation order is relied upon: the
helper calls appearing together in one printf argument list are pure, and every
per-label line passes at most one helper call, whose only argument is either an
integer constant or an already-completed read of out[0], so no call's arguments
can interact. The empty switch body is well formed and executes nothing for any
value. Each per-label runtime line is three separate full expressions -- the
volatile store, the call whose result is captured into out[0], and the printf --
so the volatile access sequence is fixed and no object is modified twice between
sequence points there either. Every subscript stays strictly inside its table:
dense_in has 18 elements read at 0 through 17, dense_off_in has 9 read at 0
through 8, and sparse_in has 8 read at 0 through 7, each loop bounded by the
literal element count.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Nothing implementation-defined is printed. Plain char is never used as a value,
which matters because char signedness was measured to differ across the four
targets: signed on x86_64 and i686, unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64. Every
printed value has type int, which is 32 bits on all four targets, so no value
depends on the measured pointer and long width difference (4 bytes on i686,
8 bytes on the other three). No address, no pointer value, no sizeof result and
no floating-point value is printed. NO LOWERING SHAPE IS REQUIRED, ASSERTED OR
OBSERVED BY ANY CELL OF THIS PROGRAM, and that is deliberate: this suite's oracles
compare stdout bytes and exit status, so the claim under test is that each
controlling value selects its own arm and yields its own result, whatever code the
backend emits and however that code differs between targets, between optimization
levels or between the two compilers oracle (a) compares. A backend is free to
dispatch through a jump table, a comparison chain, a bit test, a computed offset, or
any mixture, and free to choose differently at each optimization level, without
affecting a single line below. Label density is nevertheless why the dense,
offset-dense and sparse sets are all present: density is the property a backend
typically consults when it chooses a dispatch strategy, so writing all three puts
each case in front of it rather than testing only whichever one a single shape
happens to exercise. Which strategy any compiler then selects is a property of the
generated code rather than of the observable result: the three sets lowered
identically would still be a PASS here, a difference of generated code is not an
implementation-defined value difference, and no target restriction is needed.
Because no cell depends on generated code, all 12 are expected to produce
byte-identical stdout, and all 12 were measured to do so: 82 lines, exit status 0,
on every one of the four targets at -O0, -O1 and -O2.
Because the lowering strategy is left free, the OBSERVATION has to be complete
enough to judge any strategy, and that is what the per-label lines are for. A
dispatch table fails in a characteristic way -- two entries transposed, or the whole
table displaced by one -- and a sum over the label set cannot see it, because
100 + 101 and 101 + 100 are the same number. Every one of the sixteen dense
labels, every one of the eight offset labels and every one of the six sparse
labels therefore appears on its own line under a key naming the input that
produced it, in the constant path AND in the volatile-runtime path, together with
inputs that must reach default (dense 16 and -1, offset 208, sparse 0 and 999999,
the last two chosen to fall inside the span between labels and above the highest
label respectively). No label mapping in this program is observable only through
an aggregate: dense_sweep_total and sparse_sweep_total are retained purely as
redundant confirmation, and they earn their place by exercising the dispatch
inside a loop -- a context a compiler may restructure differently from a
straight-line call -- rather than by being the sole evidence for anything. Every
input either total covers is already printed individually above it, so a pair of
transposed table entries the sums cannot detect is still caught.
The offset set is the one whose per-label lines matter most. A strategy that
indexed after subtracting the lowest label would, if that subtraction were off by
one, shift every mapping by one -- nine wrong lines, immediately legible as a
displacement -- where a total would have changed by an amount that says nothing
about which direction or which entries were involved. Whether any compiler chooses
that strategy is not asserted here; the per-label lines are what make either answer
judgeable.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
